---
intent: hook
notes: One sentence: every diagram here is a few lines of text, drawn in the brand.
---
# How the work is shaped
A flow, a team, a loop, a stack and a choice — each written as text, drawn in the brand.

---
section: The flow
notes: A flow with a decision is Mermaid — the same text Docs, GitHub and Notion draw. The dotted line is the way back.
---
## From request to shipped

::: diagram
flowchart LR
    A([Request]) --> B[Triage]
    B --> C{Approved?}
    C -->|Yes| D[Build]
    C -->|No| E[Revise]
    E -.-> B
    D ==> F([Shipped]){.hero}
:::

---
section: The flow
notes: Top-down, the same grammar: who talks to whom. The store is a cylinder, the agent a hexagon.
---
## What runs behind it

::: diagram
graph TD
    U((User)) --> W[Web app]
    U --> M[Mobile app]
    W & M --> API[[Public API]]
    API --> S[(Store)]
    API --> AG{{Agent}}
    AG -.->|reads| S
:::

---
section: The team
notes: An org chart is a list: the indent is the hierarchy, each line a name and a role.
---
## Who does what

::: diagram {.tree}
- Operations | COO
  - Product | CPO
    - Platform
    - Mobile {.hero}
  - Sales | CRO
    - Inbound
    - Partners
  - Support | Head of care
    - Level 1
    - Level 2
:::

---
section: The loop
intent: explain
notes: A cycle: the steps turn, the center says what they make.
---
## One loop a quarter

::: diagram {.cycle}
center: Every quarter
- Listen | what customers say
- Decide | one thing that matters
- Ship | in small versions {.hero}
- Measure | what actually changed
:::

---
section: The stack
notes: A pyramid: the first item is the top, the last one what everything stands on.
---
## What a good release stands on

::: diagram {.pyramid}
- Trust | customers rely on it {.hero}
- Quality | tested before it ships
- Process | the same road every time
- Tools | one place for the work
:::

---
section: The platform
notes: A radial: a hub named by `center:`, the items around it, no order between them.
---
## One platform, its integrations

::: diagram {.radial}
center: Northwind
- Email | the inbox
- Calendar
- Chat | the messages
- CRM | the customer record {.hero}
- Files
:::

---
section: The pipeline
notes: A funnel: the widest first, each stage narrower — the numbers are the source's.
---
## A quarter of sales

::: diagram {.funnel}
- Visitors | 12 000 on the site
- Trials | 840 accounts
- Demos | 120 meetings
- Customers | 31 signed {.hero}
:::

---
section: The choice
intent: decide
notes: A matrix: four quadrants, two axes named once.
---
## Where to start

::: diagram {.matrix}
x: Low effort | High effort
y: High value | Low value
- Quick wins | do them this week {.hero}
- Big bets | plan them
- Fill-ins | when there is time
- Money pits | say no
:::

---
intent: act
notes: Who does what next — on the dark slide, the diagram turns white and yellow.
---
## Next quarter

::: diagram
flowchart LR
    A[Pick the quick wins] --> B[Plan one big bet]
    B --> C[Ship it in small versions]
    C ==> D[Review in March]{.hero}
:::
